findings.body:
`except:` with no exception class catches `BaseException`, so a Ctrl-C during the push or a `SystemExit` raised by a shutdown path is converted into a normal `return None`. The process then continues as if nothing happened, which makes shutdown and interruption unreliable and is almost never the intent of "make the push non-fatal". It also silently discards every real failure (network error, serialization error, bug in `_client.send`) with no log line, so a permanently broken metrics pipeline looks identical to a healthy one.

Catch `Exception` instead of using a bare `except`, and log the exception before returning:

    try:
        return _client.send(payload)
    except Exception:
        logger.warning("metrics push failed", exc_info=True)
        return None

